\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Distribution of inverse estimates for the domain-wall oscillator. The true value of the applied field amplitude is $H_0^*=800$~Oe. Each violin shows the distribution of 24 independent optimisation runs, with the number of DDIM steps used for sampling indicated on the horizontal axis. The median estimate is shown by horizontal bars, with the minimum and maximum values indicated by the edges of the violins. Inset: the absolute error of the estimate as a function of the number of DDIM steps. \textcolor {red}{Fix alignment of inset plot}}}{23}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dwo_violins}{{8}{23}{Distribution of inverse estimates for the domain-wall oscillator. The true value of the applied field amplitude is $H_0^*=800$~Oe. Each violin shows the distribution of 24 independent optimisation runs, with the number of DDIM steps used for sampling indicated on the horizontal axis. The median estimate is shown by horizontal bars, with the minimum and maximum values indicated by the edges of the violins. Inset: the absolute error of the estimate as a function of the number of DDIM steps. \textcolor {red}{Fix alignment of inset plot}}{figure.8}{}}
